5. Memory  hub

How much RAM you have, who is using it, and why "used" doesn't mean what you
think.

On your machine
  RAM      10.5 GiB available of 15.5 GiB (68%) · 1.1 GiB completely free
  Cache    7.5 GiB in buff/cache, 604.0 MiB of it shared (tmpfs)
  Swap     256.0 MiB used of 8.0 GiB · swappiness 60

Commands
  free -h                   RAM and swap, in human units
  vmstat 1                  memory and swap activity every second (Ctrl-C stops)
  top -o %MEM               processes sorted by memory use
  swapon --show             swap areas and how full they are
  sudo dmesg | grep -i oom  recent work of the OOM killer

Paths
  /proc/meminfo            the kernel's memory counters, read by free and top
  /proc/sys/vm/swappiness  how willing the kernel is to swap
  /proc/PID/status         memory of one process (VmRSS line)

Cards
  idk 5.1  free vs available
